Oasis theme assets -- MIT
  oasis.nvim: Copyright (c) 2025 Robert
    https://github.com/uhs-robert/oasis.nvim
    @ a3ef178fe47c69691e676a8da98ce5735c3013db

    config/bat/themes/Oasis Abyss Dark.tmTheme      (extras/bat, dark)
    config/bat/themes/Oasis Abyss Light 3.tmTheme   (extras/bat, light/3)
    config/wezterm/wezterm.lua                      (extras/wezterm, as tables)

  Local changes to the vendored files: both tmThemes are re-indented with
  spaces instead of tabs and end with a newline. In the dark one the diff
  foregrounds, which upstream sets to background shades, use Abyss Dark's
  green/red/blue: #1F3A2D -> #7FCF78 (inserted), #532E2E -> #FF7979
  (deleted), #1C1C1C -> #81C0FF (changed). In the light one the comment
  foreground #625f54 (4.49:1 on #d8d8d8) is darkened to #615e54 for WCAG
  AA. The wezterm tables drop upstream's tab_bar block (the tab bar is
  disabled).

  Two Abyss Light 3 keys miss WCAG AA on #d8d8d8 and are darkened in HSL
  lightness only wherever they are used (the derived palettes, the light
  tmTheme and nvim's palette_overrides): theme_accent #31732b -> #2e6b28
  and syntax_comment #625f54 -> #615e54.

  The Oasis palettes under config/theme/palettes.d/oasis/, oasis-aa.theme,
  the vim, television and COSMIC themes are derived from upstream's
  extras/lua-theme values through a Catppuccin-role map; the map is in
  config/theme/palettes.d/oasis/light/starship.toml.


